<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Granada War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1482–1492</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> War was the campaign of Isabella I and Ferdinand II against the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Granada, the last Muslim state in the Iberian peninsula. Fought with large armies and siege artillery, it took the emirate's towns one by one, helped by quarrels within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasrid-dynasty">Nasrid dynasty</a>. It ended when Muhammad XII surrendered Granada on 2 January 1492.</p></div>
